 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? Lovely. Make one big table for everyone, no small round ones. Fill it with chairs and ottomans so nobody has to stand. August heat is brutal. Keep the room well ventilated with fans and maybe a window open an inch or two. One big tuck shop is easier than many small ones. Make one dish everyone knows and loves. That's a winner. Maybe do one big tray bake on the Tuesday before, so everyone comes home to hot food. Keep the bedrooms for sleeping, and move the sofa into the kitchen for the night. It turns into one big sofa for everyone.",
